  "name": "Starlay Finance (Acala) empty USDC reserve liquidity-index inflation",
  "summary": "Starlay's Aave-v2-fork LendingPool adds each flash-loan premium to the liquidity index divided by the lToken supply, and lToken mint/burn convert amounts to scaled units with half-up rounding. On the USDC reserve, whose supply was a single scaled unit, the attacker ran 200 USDC flash loans that raised the index from 1.0000016e27 to 1.35e36, then used deposit/withdraw rounding to keep overvalued one-unit lUSDC collateral while recovering its USDC, and borrowed the pool's DOT and LDOT against it from a series of throwaway contracts.",
