  "notes": [
    "The LendingPool reset is configureReserves making USDC collateral (getConfiguration(USDC): LTV 0 to 7000), four blocks after the lUSDC proxy's creation; setReserveFactor(USDC, 0) at block 5336731 plays no part in premium accrual or rounding, and the later authorizeSybil calls only grant the oracle's fallback switch, which stayed off.",
    "The anchor is the first index inflation and already borrowed 135 DOT; the 55 earlier flash loans since launch were ordinary single loans, and the attacker's earlier 10 USDC round trips moved no index. Later transactions reused the inflated index; the referenced 100 LDOT borrow and repay was a fully collateralised probe.",
    "Acala's RPC returns at most 100 logs per receipt and no traces, so the loss is the DOT and LDOT reserves' depletion summed from Blockscout's full logs, priced with DefiLlama acala: quotes at each transaction."
